00:20.653 --> 00:22.780
You've grown a lot, Iori. It's been 10 years!

00:22.988 --> 00:24.031
IORI KITAHARA
(20 YEARS OLD)

00:24.240 --> 00:26.075
Yes. It's been about that long.

00:26.367 --> 00:29.286
We're family now. You don't have to be so polite.

00:29.495 --> 00:30.829
Yes, I understand.

00:31.038 --> 00:32.581
No, you don't!

00:38.545 --> 00:41.715
Dive Shop Grand Blue...

00:42.508 --> 00:44.176
Well? Great, right?

00:44.385 --> 00:46.887
I'm going to park the car,
so take a look around.

00:47.096 --> 00:48.430
Okay.

00:50.057 --> 00:54.103
Since I'm about to start college,
I decided to live with my uncle.

00:54.603 --> 00:57.106
I haven't been to this seaside town
in 10 years.

00:57.606 --> 01:00.276
The roaring sea and the blazing sun...

01:14.707 --> 01:16.333
Iori! Where are you?

01:16.542 --> 01:18.544
Here! I'm coming!

01:19.586 --> 01:21.839
I've seen her before somewhere.

01:22.589 --> 01:24.842
I wonder what kind of people I'll meet

01:25.050 --> 01:27.469
in this new environment...

01:31.598 --> 01:33.183
Out! Safe!

01:33.392 --> 01:35.102
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

01:37.021 --> 01:40.858
Be passionate, my friends

01:41.066 --> 01:44.028
Shine bright with the sun

01:44.236 --> 01:47.656
Dive into the blue sky

01:47.865 --> 01:51.952
And let summer take it all

01:55.331 --> 01:58.500
Grand Blue Dreaming

02:05.758 --> 02:09.595
Be passionate, my friends

02:09.803 --> 02:12.848
Shine bright with the sun

02:13.057 --> 02:16.143
Dive into the blue sky

02:16.352 --> 02:20.397
And let summer take it all

02:20.606 --> 02:23.400
An expanding ocean of possibilities

02:23.609 --> 02:27.446
Summer is our amore

02:27.654 --> 02:31.116
We’ll swear to the crystal clear sky

02:31.325 --> 02:34.244
Summer is in our hands

02:34.453 --> 02:38.332
Be passionate, my friends

02:38.540 --> 02:41.502
Shine bright with the sun

02:41.710 --> 02:44.963
Dive into the blue sky

02:45.172 --> 02:48.592
And let summer take it all

02:48.801 --> 02:52.763
With a cheerful heart

02:52.971 --> 02:55.766
Don’t mess with me

02:55.974 --> 02:59.228
Keep going even if you fall

02:59.436 --> 03:03.065
And let summer take it all

03:09.196 --> 03:10.906
What kind of people will I meet?

03:13.075 --> 03:14.910
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

03:16.286 --> 03:19.248
- Where's the new life I wished for...?
- Iori.

03:19.873 --> 03:21.792
Welcome to my store.

03:22.000 --> 03:25.212
Uncle! What's going on?

03:25.421 --> 03:27.756
Oh, yeah. People always tell me

03:27.965 --> 03:30.300
I don't look good in this apron.

03:30.509 --> 03:32.970
- That's not what I'm talking about!
- No?

03:33.178 --> 03:34.680
I'm talking about that!

03:36.974 --> 03:38.434
He pulled out his thing!

03:38.642 --> 03:40.144
It happens all the time.

03:40.352 --> 03:42.354
I'm going back to my parents' house!

03:42.563 --> 03:43.730
Is he homesick?

03:43.939 --> 03:45.274
Who was that?

03:45.524 --> 03:47.276
My nephew from Izu University.

03:47.526 --> 03:49.194
Your nephew goes to Izu University?

03:49.820 --> 03:51.113
That means... Tokita...

03:51.405 --> 03:52.865
You're right, Kotobuki.

03:53.365 --> 03:55.701
This is our chance to get a new member!

03:59.204 --> 04:01.790
Why are there perverts in the store?

04:04.877 --> 04:07.087
Wait, freshman!

04:07.504 --> 04:09.423
They're coming outside?

04:10.382 --> 04:12.509
Wait, freshman! Why are you running away?

04:12.718 --> 04:14.303
Of course I'm going to run away!

04:14.511 --> 04:17.181
Hey, you. You're a shy boy, aren't you?

04:17.389 --> 04:19.725
Are you aware of how you look?

04:19.933 --> 04:21.310
That doesn't matter!

04:21.518 --> 04:22.811
It does!

04:23.020 --> 04:25.481
Anyway, just listen to us!

04:26.523 --> 04:28.734
No!

04:33.530 --> 04:36.533
Welcome home, Iori. Are you still homesick?

04:37.618 --> 04:40.746
Well, all boys have to leave their parents someday.

04:40.954 --> 04:42.956
It's okay. You'll get used to it.

04:43.165 --> 04:46.543
Why are you assuming it's because I'm homesick?

04:47.002 --> 04:48.837
- Are we wrong?
- You're wrong!

04:49.046 --> 04:52.466
I ran away because you were having a naked festival!

04:52.674 --> 04:56.053
Do you think we're dressed like this because we like it?

04:56.261 --> 04:57.346
Isn't that why?

04:57.596 --> 04:59.806
- I'm not going to deny it.
- Pervert...

05:00.349 --> 05:03.435
We were playing Rock Paper Scissors
to decide who preps the tanks.

05:03.644 --> 05:06.814
- Tanks?
- It's a piece of diving equipment.

05:07.523 --> 05:09.316
Oh, I see.

05:09.858 --> 05:12.194
We were playing Rock Paper Scissors to decide.

05:13.153 --> 05:14.738
- So?
- "So"?

05:14.947 --> 05:16.823
Why were you naked for that?

05:17.115 --> 05:19.451
It's standard to get naked when you play.

05:19.660 --> 05:23.205
Don't you know how to play Rock Paper Scissors
without getting naked?

05:25.707 --> 05:27.125
I'm Ryujiro Kotobuki.

05:27.459 --> 05:29.711
I'm a junior in mechanical
engineering at Izu U.

05:29.920 --> 05:32.381
I'm Iori Kitahara. We're the same major.

05:32.589 --> 05:33.590
Oh, really?

05:34.007 --> 05:37.469
I'm so happy a classmate
from the same department is joining our club.

05:37.761 --> 05:39.805
I never said I'm joining.

05:41.223 --> 05:42.975
I can see it in your eyes.

05:43.433 --> 05:44.893
Oh, really?

05:49.565 --> 05:51.024
Are you interested in diving?

05:51.483 --> 05:53.068
- I am.
- Oh, really?

05:53.277 --> 05:55.028
But I don't plan on doing it.

05:55.362 --> 05:57.155
Why? Don't you want to try it?

05:58.282 --> 06:00.033
I can't swim.

06:02.828 --> 06:05.122
You're bad at Japanese, aren't you?

06:05.330 --> 06:06.498
What do you mean?

06:06.915 --> 06:08.750
I asked if you want to "do" it.

06:08.959 --> 06:11.044
But you answered whether you "can."

06:11.420 --> 06:13.755
But how can you dive if you can't swim?

06:14.298 --> 06:16.008
It'll work itself out.

06:16.592 --> 06:18.260
What? "It'll work itself out"?

06:18.594 --> 06:22.806
If you only stick with what you already know,
you'll never get anywhere.

06:23.015 --> 06:26.268
What's important is whether
you're interested or not.

06:36.194 --> 06:37.738
Thanks for scouting it out.

06:39.072 --> 06:40.741
I'm going to drop off the tanks.

06:40.949 --> 06:42.284
Thanks.

06:47.289 --> 06:48.624
Welcome, Iori!

06:48.832 --> 06:50.292
Yes! Nice to meet you!

06:50.500 --> 06:51.543
Nice to meet you?

06:52.294 --> 06:54.046
Did you forget about me?

06:55.297 --> 06:58.425
How could you forget your cousin?
You're so cold.

07:00.761 --> 07:02.679
Sorry, I didn't realize.

07:02.888 --> 07:04.431
It's been ten years.

07:04.973 --> 07:07.851
- Did you see Chisa already?
- No, not yet.

07:08.226 --> 07:11.980
You'll be surprised when you see her.
She got really cute.

07:12.314 --> 07:14.691
We were diving together just now.

07:15.525 --> 07:16.693
Oh, do you mean...?

07:19.237 --> 07:22.199
- Are you going to join Tokita's club?
- No.

07:22.574 --> 07:23.909
You don't like diving?

07:24.117 --> 07:26.203
I don't hate it, but...

07:26.578 --> 07:27.954
Then why not?

07:28.163 --> 07:30.332
I graduated from an all-boys high school.

07:30.540 --> 07:31.958
I want to keep my distance.

07:32.167 --> 07:33.669
Distance? From what?

07:33.877 --> 07:34.961
Well...

07:38.423 --> 07:40.967
From this all-boys high school vibe!

07:41.301 --> 07:42.969
Oh, you're back!

07:43.303 --> 07:44.680
Thanks for cleaning up.

07:44.888 --> 07:46.723
Please put on some clothes.

07:47.224 --> 07:49.142
Please take care of Iori!

07:49.518 --> 07:50.519
Got it!

07:53.271 --> 07:55.440
Today's your welcome party!

07:55.649 --> 07:56.942
Hey, wait.

07:57.150 --> 07:59.945
I don't want to join your club.
And also--

08:00.153 --> 08:01.613
Stop talking!

08:01.822 --> 08:03.907
- Listen, Iori.
- What?

08:04.116 --> 08:06.993
You always reject things before trying them.

08:07.327 --> 08:08.620
That's not true.

08:08.829 --> 08:11.790
It's true! You complain about
things you've never tried.

08:11.998 --> 08:13.166
That's not good.

08:13.375 --> 08:16.503
You said it's wrong to run naked
outside without trying it.

08:16.712 --> 08:18.797
I'm the one who's right here!

08:19.589 --> 08:23.135
Just drink this. We'll start with
naked Rock Paper Scissors.

08:23.468 --> 08:24.803
Experience is everything.

08:25.011 --> 08:27.472
That's something I don't need to experience!

08:27.931 --> 08:30.976
There's no such thing as a useless experience.

08:31.184 --> 08:32.936
Believe me. Just try it.

08:33.145 --> 08:34.438
I refuse.

08:34.646 --> 08:37.274
- Can you make an exception?
- There's nothing to lose.

08:37.858 --> 08:41.778
I'm not doing it!
I'm not getting dragged into your shenanigans.

08:45.949 --> 08:47.242
That was Iori, right?

08:47.451 --> 08:48.785
CHISA KOTEGAWA
(20 YEARS OLD)

08:54.166 --> 08:55.584
It's been ten years...

09:03.133 --> 09:05.927
You're no match for me!

09:06.136 --> 09:07.637
Wow, Iori!

09:07.846 --> 09:09.931
You beat three guys! I'm impressed!

09:10.140 --> 09:13.435
Beat me if you can! I want to show off my massive rod!

09:13.643 --> 09:16.480
- Look who's talking!
- I bet it's a toothpick!

09:16.938 --> 09:19.524
Bring it on! My trunks are going nowhere!

09:19.733 --> 09:21.818
Oh, Chisa. Welcome home.

09:22.152 --> 09:23.153
I'm back.

09:30.368 --> 09:32.954
Hey. Long time no see, Chisa.

09:33.288 --> 09:34.748
Do you remember me?

09:39.127 --> 09:40.879
We have to throw this away now.

09:41.087 --> 09:43.006
My hand's not that dirty!

09:43.882 --> 09:47.969
I never imagined you'd grow up to be so stupid.

09:48.178 --> 09:51.515
That's not true!

09:52.390 --> 09:53.892
Why is this happening?

09:54.267 --> 09:56.269
You're Chisa's cousin, right?

09:56.603 --> 09:59.397
You're so lucky you live with your cute cousin.

09:59.689 --> 10:03.109
She just treated me like a piece of crap.

10:04.069 --> 10:07.656
But it's okay.
Nanaka's living in the same house!

10:09.366 --> 10:11.409
Just give up now, Iori.

10:12.077 --> 10:13.370
What do you mean?

10:13.578 --> 10:19.417
Nanaka's hiding it,
and the person involved still doesn't know, but...

10:24.923 --> 10:27.175
She's in love with her sister.

10:27.384 --> 10:29.427
What happened in the last ten years?

10:30.220 --> 10:34.057
I can't take it. She was the only person today
who was nice to me.

10:34.432 --> 10:39.646
Don't worry about it.
Most people don't have a perfect life at home.

10:40.105 --> 10:42.357
Well, you're right.

10:42.691 --> 10:45.318
You can't expect your home life
to be like a drama.

10:45.527 --> 10:46.611
Right.

10:46.820 --> 10:49.781
I'm going to work at having a good college life
instead!

10:49.990 --> 10:51.575
You're on fire!

10:54.119 --> 10:57.372
- Let's have an after-party!
- Yeah!

10:57.581 --> 11:02.085
- I'm going home. I have to work early tomorrow.
- I gotta catch the train too.

11:02.460 --> 11:03.753
I'm leaving too.

11:03.962 --> 11:06.339
You don't have to catch a train, right?

11:06.548 --> 11:07.841
You live right here.

11:08.300 --> 11:11.595
Hold on! I have orientation at 9 a.m. tomorrow!

11:11.845 --> 11:14.723
You'll be okay. Leave it to us.

11:14.931 --> 11:17.309
We'll make sure you aren't late.

11:28.904 --> 11:30.488
My head hurts.

11:31.281 --> 11:33.533
It's because I went to their party.

11:34.492 --> 11:35.869
What time is it?

11:36.494 --> 11:38.622
I'm going to be late!

11:48.965 --> 11:50.383
AUDITORIUM

11:50.800 --> 11:53.595
See? You definitely won't be late.

11:53.845 --> 11:56.348
You idiots!

11:59.976 --> 12:01.728
IZU UNIVERSITY

12:02.187 --> 12:06.983
I was filled with hope.
Meeting new people. Starting a new life.

12:07.192 --> 12:10.028
That's the guy who was passed out
in front of the auditorium.

12:10.236 --> 12:12.989
Everything was covered in clouds of grey
on the first day.

12:13.323 --> 12:16.242
- Hey, that guy...
- He's kind of hot.

12:17.202 --> 12:19.037
KOHEI IMAMURA
(20 YEARS OLD)

12:22.248 --> 12:23.875
He is good-look--

12:32.467 --> 12:35.303
I'm going to stay away from that guy.

12:36.054 --> 12:37.555
That's all for today.

12:38.098 --> 12:40.934
- Let's go check out clubs.
- Where do we go first?

12:42.102 --> 12:43.812
Checking out clubs...

12:46.606 --> 12:49.067
Chisa. Are you going to check out any clubs?

12:49.484 --> 12:50.527
Hey!

12:52.153 --> 12:54.322
Don't talk to me dressed like that.

12:55.323 --> 12:56.658
Now that you mention it...

12:57.617 --> 13:00.412
I want to get dressed,
but I don't know the way home.

13:00.829 --> 13:02.288
I'm going home now.

13:02.497 --> 13:03.790
Yeah, let's go!

13:04.040 --> 13:05.875
Why are you following me?

13:06.251 --> 13:08.003
I thought you could show me the way.

13:08.211 --> 13:10.171
- No way.
- Why?

13:10.422 --> 13:12.090
Do I have to spell it out for you?

13:12.298 --> 13:13.675
No. I sort of know why.

13:13.925 --> 13:16.219
Well, I hope you know exactly why.

13:17.387 --> 13:19.347
Well, then. I'm going home now.

13:19.931 --> 13:22.434
I know you don't want to go home with me.

13:22.809 --> 13:24.519
But I have a problem.

13:24.811 --> 13:26.730
Can you give me your clothes?

13:27.105 --> 13:30.066
A half-naked pervert
demanded I hand over my clothes.

13:30.275 --> 13:33.111
Wait! We're cousins, right?

13:33.319 --> 13:35.238
My problems are your problems!

13:35.447 --> 13:39.200
Your clothes are my clothes!
We help each other out, right?

13:39.409 --> 13:42.954
Just stop.
Don't say stuff like that so loudly.

13:43.163 --> 13:46.249
- Stuff like that?
- Like that we're cousins.

13:48.585 --> 13:50.503
I get it. Then...

13:51.004 --> 13:55.216
If you don't give me your clothes,
I'm going to tell everyone we live together.

13:59.304 --> 14:00.513
All right.

14:01.264 --> 14:03.600
I'll take them off. I'll take off my clothes.

14:04.392 --> 14:05.602
Please.

14:06.019 --> 14:08.521
Don't tell anyone about my home situation.

14:08.938 --> 14:14.110
Hold on. This sounds like a crime scene.

14:20.116 --> 14:22.660
Did you see a suspicious half-naked man?

14:23.703 --> 14:25.789
What did I do wrong?

14:26.331 --> 14:27.707
What are you doing?

14:29.084 --> 14:30.627
Oh, it's just you.

14:32.378 --> 14:34.005
It's complicated.

14:34.214 --> 14:37.175
I could help you out. But it depends.

14:37.634 --> 14:39.969
You're actually a good guy!

14:40.178 --> 14:43.515
I'm Kohei Imamura. So, what happened?

14:43.848 --> 14:48.686
Listen to me! Chisa wouldn't take me home with her
and wouldn't even take off her clothes.

14:48.895 --> 14:51.940
- Guard!
- Give me one more chance, please!

14:52.315 --> 14:55.735
Stalking and obscene acts.
You can't make excuses for that.

14:55.944 --> 14:57.445
There's a good reason.

14:57.654 --> 15:00.949
Then talk about your reason in jail.

15:01.825 --> 15:03.284
- Bye.
- Wait!

15:03.618 --> 15:05.745
That's enough talk. Instead...

15:07.205 --> 15:08.873
Take off your clothes.

15:14.045 --> 15:15.046
Where did he go?

15:15.755 --> 15:18.174
- That bastard.
- Pervert!

15:18.967 --> 15:21.761
But I still have to find some clothes.

15:21.970 --> 15:24.305
Who else do I know?

15:28.184 --> 15:31.104
We're from the diving club, Peek-a-Boo!

15:31.604 --> 15:32.605
Where is he?

15:33.148 --> 15:34.607
You'll be okay now.

15:35.984 --> 15:37.110
Thanks for your help.

15:37.652 --> 15:38.862
So? What's up?

15:39.237 --> 15:40.780
Can I borrow some clothes?

15:41.364 --> 15:43.366
What a weird thing to say.

15:43.950 --> 15:46.536
We're going for drinks later. It'd be a waste of time.

15:46.828 --> 15:50.498
Are you assuming
I'm going to take off my clothes when I drink?

15:51.291 --> 15:53.751
We're having our freshman welcome party today!

15:53.960 --> 15:56.754
That's nice. But I need some clothes.

15:57.088 --> 16:01.092
Then if you can get a freshman to join,
I'll let you borrow some clothes.

16:02.051 --> 16:04.429
- You're on!
- Do you have any leads?

16:04.637 --> 16:06.472
Leave it to me.

16:14.814 --> 16:16.774
Damn! Why?

16:17.192 --> 16:22.530
Why isn't there a club with a harem of high school girls
who worship me?

16:24.949 --> 16:27.535
- You?
- Don't give up, Kohei.

16:28.494 --> 16:30.496
Never quit. Your dreams will come true.

16:30.705 --> 16:32.665
That's how the world works.

16:33.583 --> 16:36.169
But reality is harsh.

16:37.921 --> 16:44.385
Everyone tells me I'm dreaming and says
there aren't any high-school girls in college!

16:44.802 --> 16:50.266
I thought if I went to college, the life I dreamed of
would be waiting for me!

16:50.683 --> 16:51.684
It is.

16:52.477 --> 16:57.690
You just haven't noticed the door
to the life of your dreams.

16:58.483 --> 17:00.485
Really?

17:01.069 --> 17:04.697
What do you say?
Let's open the door to our dreams together!

17:10.119 --> 17:12.038
Welcome!

17:12.247 --> 17:13.957
You tricked me! Bastard!

17:15.375 --> 17:17.961
Clothes are one of man's best inventions.

17:18.336 --> 17:21.965
- Let's start the freshman welcome party.
- Yeah!

17:22.257 --> 17:23.800
Iori, what do you want to drink?

17:24.175 --> 17:25.718
Oolong tea, please.

17:25.927 --> 17:27.220
Okay. I got it.

17:27.428 --> 17:29.013
VODKA: 9

17:29.222 --> 17:30.682
WHISKEY: 1

17:30.890 --> 17:32.308
Here. Oolong tea.

17:32.517 --> 17:33.893
That's not oolong tea!

17:34.102 --> 17:35.395
THIS IS EXTREMELY DANGEROUS. DO NOT
ATTEMPT TO RECREATE OR RE-ENACT THIS ACTIVITY.

17:35.603 --> 17:38.731
What are you talking about?
It's the same color.

17:39.232 --> 17:40.733
Not only the color.

17:41.526 --> 17:42.735
You can light it on fire.

17:43.027 --> 17:45.738
If you can light it on fire, that means it's alcohol!

17:46.030 --> 17:47.407
Then do you want some water?

17:53.413 --> 17:55.039
How come you can light it on fire?

17:55.248 --> 17:56.541
It's combustible.

17:56.874 --> 17:58.543
Stop worrying. It's the same color.

17:58.751 --> 18:02.005
Is color the only way you can tell drinks apart?

18:04.424 --> 18:05.675
Here we go!

18:06.175 --> 18:07.844
Bottoms up!

18:08.052 --> 18:11.014
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

18:18.938 --> 18:20.606
Chisa, I didn't know you were here.

18:21.816 --> 18:23.192
My dad told me to come.

18:23.568 --> 18:25.111
Are you joining this club?

18:25.570 --> 18:27.613
Yeah, unfortunately.
How about you?

18:27.822 --> 18:29.282
I'm going to say no.

18:30.700 --> 18:31.784
Are you sure you can?

18:37.415 --> 18:40.793
Hey, Iori. Make sure you drink.

18:41.002 --> 18:42.170
Wait. No!

18:43.671 --> 18:44.672
Idiot.

18:45.340 --> 18:46.799
Bottoms up!

18:47.008 --> 18:48.176
Cheers!

18:51.095 --> 18:52.180
That was strong!

18:52.555 --> 18:54.557
Have some water, or else you'll pass out!

18:55.099 --> 18:56.184
Oh, thanks.

19:02.357 --> 19:04.692
Vodka!

19:05.026 --> 19:07.403
You drink a lot, Iori Kitahara.

19:07.612 --> 19:10.573
Kohei! Are you trying to get revenge on me?

19:10.782 --> 19:12.700
Of course not. But...

19:13.326 --> 19:17.205
If I don't get someone else drunk and
make them join the club, I'll never get away.

19:17.789 --> 19:21.459
I see. Someone's got to be the victim.

19:21.959 --> 19:23.211
You understand me?

19:23.419 --> 19:26.214
Yeah. I'm responsible for bringing you here.

19:27.131 --> 19:30.468
I'll drink, so you just have some oolong tea.

19:31.427 --> 19:34.472
What a beautiful act of self-sacrifice.

19:40.645 --> 19:41.646
Bastard!

19:41.854 --> 19:45.441
Who says that I'm the one who has to be the victim?

19:45.775 --> 19:47.485
You evil bastard!

19:47.819 --> 19:49.737
Hey, hey, don't fight.

19:50.113 --> 19:51.989
If you want to fight, have a match.

19:52.448 --> 19:53.491
A match?

19:54.784 --> 19:56.994
A PaB staring contest.

19:57.286 --> 20:01.499
The rules are simple. Whoever sprays their drink
first loses. That's all.

20:01.791 --> 20:02.792
I got it.

20:04.168 --> 20:08.881
Time for a staring contest! Peek-a-Boo!

20:16.472 --> 20:19.725
Kohei. One strategy is to talk about something serious.

20:20.059 --> 20:22.019
- Something serious?
- Yeah.

20:22.353 --> 20:26.274
People laugh when they're not supposed to.

20:26.732 --> 20:27.733
I get it.

20:28.067 --> 20:30.278
Then I'm going to talk about my problems.

20:31.320 --> 20:32.780
Just between us,

20:33.072 --> 20:34.407
to tell you the truth, I...

20:35.199 --> 20:37.618
I used to be an otaku.

20:39.203 --> 20:41.664
Seems like you couldn't hide your surprise.

20:42.206 --> 20:45.042
You're the one who can't hide that you're an otaku!

20:45.251 --> 20:46.961
Iori, you're so careless.

20:48.087 --> 20:49.714
Damn!

20:52.592 --> 20:56.220
Time for a staring contest! Peek-a-Boo!

20:56.429 --> 20:57.430
Iori.

20:58.222 --> 20:59.932
Hey, are you okay?

21:00.266 --> 21:02.393
I want to play basketball.

21:04.103 --> 21:06.689
Yes!
I'm going to make you drink too!

21:08.357 --> 21:11.194
You're being careless again, Iori.

21:15.031 --> 21:17.783
- Look what you did!
- You bastard!

21:17.992 --> 21:19.744
I'm going to make you pay!

21:19.952 --> 21:22.705
Fine! Let's settle this once and for all!

21:23.080 --> 21:27.752
Time for a staring contest! Peek-a-Boo!

21:32.798 --> 21:34.800
Come on, guys.

21:35.843 --> 21:37.261
- Here.
- Water.

21:37.470 --> 21:38.513
Thanks.

21:39.096 --> 21:40.765
That was unexpected.

21:45.353 --> 21:48.022
I didn't know you guys wanted to drink so bad.

21:48.231 --> 21:50.024
ALCOHOL 96%

21:50.608 --> 21:53.528
I hope this'll be enough to satisfy you!

21:55.988 --> 21:59.033
This isn't water!

22:04.580 --> 22:07.917
I heard Iori's joining the club with his friend.

22:08.376 --> 22:10.169
- Good.
- Yeah.

22:10.836 --> 22:13.214
But he spent two nights out in a row.

22:13.548 --> 22:15.174
We should say something.

22:20.596 --> 22:22.431
It's your fault.

22:22.765 --> 22:24.934
No. It's your fault.

22:28.980 --> 22:31.107
What an idiot.

22:32.191 --> 22:33.401
DEEP BLUE AL FINE
KAYA MIZUKI

22:33.609 --> 22:35.695
Here’s your mic, Kitahara.

22:35.903 --> 22:39.949
Me, too...? Alright, let’s do this!

22:40.241 --> 22:43.452
- Yeah, sing your heart out.
- You guys seem to be having fun.

22:45.121 --> 22:51.127
A fairytale whispers
In a fake world

22:51.335 --> 22:57.049
Hiding in the complete darkness

22:57.258 --> 23:03.014
I reach for the forbidden fruit
In my last days

23:03.222 --> 23:09.312
Now I know the meaning of the song about hope

23:09.520 --> 23:14.567
A broken gear will never stop again

23:14.775 --> 23:22.158
Even if I were to lose everything
I’d still want you to know

23:22.366 --> 23:28.247
Trapped in the sky so far away
I’m praying with ripped off wings

23:28.456 --> 23:34.211
Because we span together
The vows of areppegio

23:34.420 --> 23:40.134
If life sparkles only to the beat
of the resonating stars

23:40.343 --> 23:43.137
I’ll sacrifice everything

23:43.346 --> 23:47.683
Till death do us apart

23:47.892 --> 23:49.769
Cheers!

23:54.565 --> 23:57.193
We’re very sorry!

24:02.406 --> 24:04.575
A women's college?

24:04.867 --> 24:06.452
Please, Nanaka!

24:06.661 --> 24:08.454
I know you want to have fun, but...

24:08.663 --> 24:09.705
But, captain!

24:09.914 --> 24:12.041
- No!
- Please!

24:12.249 --> 24:13.668
No means no!

24:14.418 --> 24:16.921
NEXT EPISODE
"UNDERWATER"
